---
import { withBase } from "../lib/paths";
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About this site" section="Colophon">
  <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The colophon</p><h1>A small, quiet website<span class="accent">.</span></h1><p>Built around the writing.</p></header>
  <div class="prose"><p>This blog is inspired by <a href="https://stephango.com/">Steph Ango’s personal site</a> and the simplicity of Obsidian’s Minimal theme: readable pages, connected ideas, and very little getting in the way.</p><h2>Under the hood</h2><p>Posts are ordinary Markdown files. <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a> turns them into static pages. Search runs in your browser, and your theme preference stays on your device.</p><p>There are no advertising scripts, analytics trackers, or external font requests in the site.</p><h2>A note on the content</h2><p>The initial essays are illustrative sample content, labeled on each post. They are starting points for the blog, rather than accounts of Maverick’s personal experience.</p><h2>Keep in touch with the writing</h2><p>Add the <a href={withBase("/rss.xml")}>RSS feed</a> to your reader for new notes.</p></div>
</Layout>
